\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Error accumulation analysis over $10^5$ seconds with flux tolerance $\varepsilon _{\mathrm  {flux}} = 10^{-6}$. (a) Relative error in mean of species $C$ decays from $0.1\%$ to $0.015\%$ as the distribution spreads. (b) Instantaneous error rate remains approximately constant at $4.9 \times 10^{-7}$ s$^{-1}$ throughout the stable region. (c) Mean trajectories for species $C$ (full FSP vs.\ adaptive) and species $A$ (reference). (d) Absolute error scales linearly with mean population: $\epsilon \approx 1.11 \times 10^{-4} \langle C \rangle $, corresponding to $0.01\%$ relative error.\relax }}{21}{figure.caption.159}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:error_accumulation}{{6}{21}{Error accumulation analysis over $10^5$ seconds with flux tolerance $\varepsilon _{\mathrm {flux}} = 10^{-6}$. (a) Relative error in mean of species $C$ decays from $0.1\%$ to $0.015\%$ as the distribution spreads. (b) Instantaneous error rate remains approximately constant at $4.9 \times 10^{-7}$ s$^{-1}$ throughout the stable region. (c) Mean trajectories for species $C$ (full FSP vs.\ adaptive) and species $A$ (reference). (d) Absolute error scales linearly with mean population: $\epsilon \approx 1.11 \times 10^{-4} \langle C \rangle $, corresponding to $0.01\%$ relative error.\relax }{figure.caption.159}{}}
