\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Adaptive FSP simulation of the Robertson system over eight decades of time ($10^{-5}$ to $10^5$ s). (a) Mean population trajectories for species $A$ (solid), $B$ (dashed), and $C$ (dotted) showing three-phase dynamics: slow initiation, explosive autocatalysis, and protracted equilibration. (b) Dynamic state space size achieving $\sim 10^4:1$ compression relative to the theoretical space of $3 \times 10^7$ states. (c) Adaptive time step spanning seven orders of magnitude in response to changing flux. (d) Total flux tracking system activity and guiding both time step and state space adaptation.\relax }}{27}{figure.caption.173}\protected@file@percent }
